[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) holds more than one bug. The desk merged its reports by subject line
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and different bugs produce the same
subjects. Each problem below now has its own ticket, with the reports it covers.

<Callout kind="warn">
Fixing the parser closes only the first ticket. The other two need their own fixes.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How each report was placed

1. **parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Every tenant on file writes the
   day first, so the day and the month swap.
2. **hint.** The booking-v3 form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type month
   first, as told, and the form reads the date day first. Only reports typed into that form
   from a booking-v3 tenant count here.
3. **one-day move.** The booking moves by one day, or lands on different days in different
   time zones. Nothing swaps. These are the reports the desk listed as a one-day move.

A report goes to its problem by tenant and channel, as `causes.ts` decides, not by the intake
tag. Intake guesses from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant on many of
these reports.

## For the desk

- A shared subject line does not mean a shared cause. Check tenant and channel before you merge.
- Read the body when a report does not describe a swap. The one-day moves were already in the
  desk notes.

